<title>AUSTRIA: ALPINE SKIING-FRITZ STROBL WINS WORLD CUP DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-FRITZ STROBL WINS WORLD CUP DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>KITZBUEHEL, Austria 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Fritz Strobl won a men's Alpine skiing World Cup downhill race on Saturday with a time of one minute 51.58 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>His team mate Werner Franz finished second in 1:52.15 and Luc Alphand of France was third with a time of 1:52.20.</p>
</text>
